{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md | sed -n '32,95p;108,130p'\"","aggregated_output":"    32\t## 2. Requirements\n    33\t\n    34\t### Functional\n    35\t- R1: A spec shall be able to declare `### Accepted limits` entries with stable ids (`L<N>`), each naming the assumption and why it is accepted.\n    36\t- R2: The review brief shall list the declared limits and instruct the reviewer to classify a finding that falls inside one as a follow-up naming the limit, or to dispute the limit explicitly.\n    37\t- R3: The conclusion and the attestation shall record which findings were classified under which limit.\n    38\t- R4: `lint-spec --ready-check` shall require accepted limits to be justified and the ADR, when present, to reference them.\n    39\t\n    40\t### Non-functional\n    41\tExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n    42\t\n    43\t### Security\n    44\tNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n    45\t\n    46\t### Compatibility\n    47\tRecords and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n    48\t\n    49\t## 3. Technical Plan\n    50\t\n    51\t### Affected areas\n    52\t`pose-mcp` (CLI and engine), the manual and its embedded copy.\n    53\t\n    54\t### Artifacts\n    55\t- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md\n    56\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\n    57\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits_test.go\n    58\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n    59\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n    60\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\n    61\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n    62\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\n    63\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n    64\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go\n    65\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_versions_test.go\n    66\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go\n    67\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\n    68\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\n    69\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/accepted_limits_lint_test.go\n    70\t- modified: POSE.md\n    71\t- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n    72\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n    73\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\t### Delivery targets\n    77\t\n    78\t- capability:review-declared-threat-model module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t### Accepted limits\n    82\t- L1: The limits are written by the implementer, so a limit can be broader than it should be. Accepted because the brief presents them as data to verify and a disputed limit is a blocking finding of its own.\n    83\t- L2: A spec edited after sealing changes its limits only through a new bundle. Accepted because the limits enter the plan digest, so an edit stales the review as any other change does.\n    84\t\n    85\t### API/contract changes\n    86\tA spec section `### Accepted limits` with `- L<N>: <assumption>. Accepted because <reason>.` entries. The review plan and the bundle seal them as `accepted_limits` (omitted when none, so every other plan and bundle keeps its digest). A draft finding may carry `limit`; the attestation records it with disposition `within-limit`. Brief template `review-brief/11`. `lint-spec --ready-check` checks the section.\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t### Data/storage changes\n    90\t`accepted_limits` in review plans and bundles and `limit` in draft and attestation findings, all omitted when empty.\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t### Technical risks\n    94\tA limit could be used to wave a real defect through. It is the spec's own declaration, sealed into the plan digest and visible in the brief and the attestation; the reviewer may dispute it with a finding of its own, which then blocks as any finding does.\n    95\t\n   108\t## 5. Decisions\n   109\t\n   110\t### Decision D1\n   111\t- Basis: R1, R2, R3\n   112\tA finding inside a declared limit is neither an open finding nor an accepted risk: it gets its own disposition, `within-limit`, which does not block an approval whatever its severity, requires a sealed limit and a reason, and records the limit's id. Accepted risks keep their severity bound; a limit is the spec's statement of scope, decided before the review.\n   113\t\n   114\t### Decision D2\n   115\t- Basis: R1, R4\n   116\tThe limits are sealed in the plan and the bundle, and in the plan digest, so the brief and the conclusion read them from what was reviewed, never from the current spec; both fields are omitted when empty so no earlier plan or bundle changes digest.\n   117\t\n   118\t## 6. Validation\n   119\t\n   120\t### Strategy\n   121\tEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n   122\t\n   123\t### Deterministic checks\n   124\t\n   125\t#### Test\n   126\t- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n   127\t\n   128\t### Execution log\n   129\t- 2026-11-25: implemented R1–R4: `ParseAcceptedLimits`, the plan and bundle `accepted_limits`, the draft `limit` and the `within-limit` disposition, `review-brief/11` and the ready check. Each has a test that fails with it mutated out; the first digest test survived because the spec edit changed the scope digest too, and now compares the plan's digest with and without the limits.\n   130\t- 2026-11-25: review round 1 (rrn-d1680df442b23d12) requested changes. N1: in a scope with several specs (a milestone or a roadmap) each limit id is qualified by its spec as `<spec>#L<N>`, with the spec recorded, so a finding names exactly one sealed limit. N2: the reason must follow `Accepted because`, not only the marker. N3: an ADR names a limit only by the id as a word, so L10 does not name L1. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits_test.go; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/accepted_limits_lint_test.go'","aggregated_output":"     1\tpackage pose\n     2\t\n     3\timport (\n     4\t\t\"os\"\n     5\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n     6\t\t\"strings\"\n     7\t\t\"testing\"\n     8\t)\n     9\t\n    10\tconst limitsSection = `\n    11\t### Accepted limits\n    12\t- L1: A process that clears its environment escapes. Accepted because the shim covers it.\n    13\t- L2: Windows is untested here. Accepted because the host is Linux.\n    14\t`\n    15\t\n    16\t// Spec pose-review-declared-threat-model R1: the section is read as\n    17\t// written, and what does not say why it is accepted is reported.\n    18\tfunc TestAcceptedLimitsAreParsed(t *testing.T) {\n    19\t\tlimits, problems := ParseAcceptedLimits(\"## 3. Technical Plan\\n\" + limitsSection + \"\\n### Other\\n- L9: not a limit here.\\n\")\n    20\t\tif len(problems) != 0 || len(limits) != 2 || limits[0].ID != \"L1\" || limits[1].ID != \"L2\" {\n    21\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"limits %+v problems %v\", limits, problems)\n    22\t\t}\n    23\t\t_, problems = ParseAcceptedLimits(\"### Accepted limits\\n- L1: no reason given.\\n- L1: twice. Accepted because yes.\\n- X1: wrong id. Accepted because no.\\n- L3: a marker with nothing after it. Accepted because\\n\")\n    24\t\tjoined := strings.Join(problems, \"\\n\")\n    25\t\tfor _, want := range []string{\"L1 does not say why it is accepted\", \"L1 is declared twice\", \"is not written as\", \"L3 does not say why it is accepted\"} {\n    26\t\t\tif !strings.Contains(joined, want) {\n    27\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"missing problem %q in %v\", want, problems)\n    28\t\t\t}\n    29\t\t}\n    30\t}\n    31\t\n    32\t// R1: the review plan seals the limits the spec declares, and they enter the\n    33\t// plan digest; a spec without limits keeps its digest.\n    34\tfunc TestTheReviewPlanSealsTheAcceptedLimits(t *testing.T) {\n    35\t\troot, store := reviewBundleFixture(t)\n    36\t\tbefore, err := store.ReviewPlan(\"spec:backend\")\n    37\t\tif err != nil || len(before.AcceptedLimits) != 0 {\n    38\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"plan without limits: %+v %v\", before.AcceptedLimits, err)\n    39\t\t}\n    40\t\tpath := filepath.Join(root, \".pose/specs/backend/spec.md\")\n    41\t\traw, _ := os.ReadFile(path)\n    42\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(path, []byte(strings.Replace(string(raw), \"### Technical risks\", strings.TrimPrefix(limitsSection, \"\\n\")+\"\\n### Technical risks\", 1)), 0o644); err != nil {\n    43\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    44\t\t}\n    45\t\tafter, err := store.ReviewPlan(\"spec:backend\")\n    46\t\tif err != nil || len(after.AcceptedLimits) != 2 || after.AcceptedLimits[0].ID != \"L1\" {\n    47\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"plan with limits: %+v %v\", after.AcceptedLimits, err)\n    48\t\t}\n    49\t\twithout := after\n    50\t\twithout.AcceptedLimits = nil\n    51\t\tif digest, err := digestReviewPlan(without); err != nil || digest == after.PlanDigest {\n    52\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the accepted limits did not enter the plan digest: %v\", err)\n    53\t\t}\n    54\t}\n    55\t\n    56\t// R2, R3: a follow-up the reviewer classifies inside a sealed limit is\n    57\t// recorded within-limit, naming it, and does not block an approval whatever\n    58\t// its severity; a limit the bundle did not seal accepts nothing.\n    59\tfunc TestAFindingWithinASealedLimitDoesNotBlockApproval(t *testing.T) {\n    60\t\tvar bundle ReviewBundle\n    61\t\tbundle.Payload.Plan.AcceptedLimits = []ReviewAcceptedLimit{{ID: \"L1\", Text: \"x. Accepted because y.\"}}\n    62\t\tdraft := ReviewDraft{Decision: \"approved\", Findings: []ReviewDraftFinding{\n    63\t\t\t{ID: \"N1\", Severity: \"high\", Disposition: \"follow-up\", Summary: \"an orphan that clears its environment escapes; that is L1\", Limit: \"L1\"},\n    64\t\t}}\n    65\t\tatt := reviewAttestationFromDraft(ReviewRun{RunID: \"rrn-0000000000000001\"}, bundle, draft, \"agent:reviewer\")\n    66\t\tif len(att.Findings) != 1 || att.Findings[0].Disposition != \"within-limit\" || att.Findings[0].Limit != \"L1\" {\n    67\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the finding was not recorded within its limit: %+v\", att.Findings)\n    68\t\t}\n    69\t\tatt.Decision = \"approved\"\n    70\t\tif blockers := reviewFindingDecisionBlockers(bundle, att); len(blockers) != 0 {\n    71\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a finding within a sealed limit blocked the approval: %v\", blockers)\n    72\t\t}\n    73\t\tatt.Findings[0].Limit = \"L9\"\n    74\t\tif blockers := strings.Join(reviewFindingDecisionBlockers(bundle, att), \"\\n\"); !strings.Contains(blockers, \"L9, which this bundle did not seal\") {\n    75\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an unsealed limit was accepted: %s\", blockers)\n    76\t\t}\n    77\t\tatt.Findings[0].Limit, att.Findings[0].Rationale = \"L1\", \"\"\n    78\t\tif blockers := strings.Join(reviewFindingDecisionBlockers(bundle, att), \"\\n\"); !strings.Contains(blockers, \"without saying why\") {\n    79\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a finding within a limit without a reason was accepted: %s\", blockers)\n    80\t\t}\n    81\t}\n    82\t\n    83\t// Review round 1, N1: across the specs of a composite scope each limit is\n    84\t// qualified by its spec, so a finding names exactly one.\n    85\tfunc TestLimitsAcrossSpecsAreQualified(t *testing.T) {\n    86\t\tbody := \"### Accepted limits\\n- L1: one. Accepted because it is rare.\\n\"\n    87\t\tsingle := acceptedLimitsOfSpecs([]Spec{{Slug: \"alpha\", Body: body}})\n    88\t\tif len(single) != 1 || single[0].ID != \"L1\" || single[0].Spec != \"\" {\n    89\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a single spec's limit was qualified: %+v\", single)\n    90\t\t}\n    91\t\tboth := acceptedLimitsOfSpecs([]Spec{{Slug: \"alpha\", Body: body}, {Slug: \"beta\", Body: body}})\n    92\t\tif len(both) != 2 || both[0].ID != \"alpha#L1\" || both[1].ID != \"beta#L1\" || both[1].Spec != \"beta\" {\n    93\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"limits across specs are ambiguous: %+v\", both)\n    94\t\t}\n    95\t}\n     1\tpackage cli\n     2\t\n     3\timport (\n     4\t\t\"bytes\"\n     5\t\t\"os\"\n     6\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n     7\t\t\"strings\"\n     8\t\t\"testing\"\n     9\t)\n    10\t\n    11\t// Spec pose-review-declared-threat-model R4: the ready check refuses an\n    12\t// accepted limit without its reason, and one an ADR citing the spec omits.\n    13\tfunc TestReadyCheckJudgesAcceptedLimits(t *testing.T) {\n    14\t\troot := t.TempDir()\n    15\t\twrite := func(rel, body string) {\n    16\t\t\tp := filepath.Join(root, rel)\n    17\t\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(p), 0o755); err != nil {\n    18\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    19\t\t\t}\n    20\t\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(p, []byte(body), 0o644); err != nil {\n    21\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    22\t\t\t}\n    23\t\t}\n    24\t\tspec := func(limits string) string {\n    25\t\t\treturn \"---\\nslug: limited\\nstatus: draft\\ncreated_at: 2026-11-25\\n---\\n\\n# Spec: limited\\n\\n## 1. Intent\\n\\n### Goal\\nA goal worth stating.\\n\\n## 2. Requirements\\n\\n### Functional\\n- R1: It works.\\n\\n## 3. Technical Plan\\n\\n### Affected areas\\nThe engine.\\n\" + limits + \"\\n## 4. Tasks\\n- [ ] Do it.\\n\"\n    26\t\t}\n    27\t\tpath := filepath.Join(root, \".pose/specs/limited/spec.md\")\n    28\t\trun := func() (int, string) {\n    29\t\t\tvar out, errOut bytes.Buffer\n    30\t\t\tcode := lintOneSpec(path, false, true, &out, &errOut)\n    31\t\t\treturn code, out.String() + errOut.String()\n    32\t\t}\n    33\t\twrite(\".pose/specs/limited/spec.md\", spec(\"\\n### Accepted limits\\n- L1: an escape. Accepted because it is rare.\\n\"))\n    34\t\tif code, out := run(); code != 0 {\n    35\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a justified limit failed the ready check: %d %s\", code, out)\n    36\t\t}\n    37\t\twrite(\".pose/specs/limited/spec.md\", spec(\"\\n### Accepted limits\\n- L1: an escape with no reason.\\n\"))\n    38\t\tif code, out := run(); code == 0 || !strings.Contains(out, \"does not say why it is accepted\") {\n    39\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an unjustified limit passed: %d %s\", code, out)\n    40\t\t}\n    41\t\twrite(\".pose/specs/limited/spec.md\", spec(\"\\n### Accepted limits\\n- L1: an escape. Accepted because it is rare.\\n- L2: another. Accepted because it is rarer.\\n\"))\n    42\t\t// Review round 1, N3: L10 does not name L1.\n    43\t\twrite(\".pose/adr/2026-11-25-limited.md\", \"# ADR\\n\\nFor `limited`. L10 and L2 are accepted.\\n\")\n    44\t\tif code, out := run(); code == 0 || !strings.Contains(out, \"accepted limit L1 is not named by the ADR\") {\n    45\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"L10 was taken as naming L1: %d %s\", code, out)\n    46\t\t}\n    47\t\twrite(\".pose/adr/2026-11-25-limited.md\", \"# ADR\\n\\nFor `limited`. L1 is accepted.\\n\")\n    48\t\tif code, out := run(); code == 0 || !strings.Contains(out, \"accepted limit L2 is not named by the ADR\") {\n    49\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a limit the ADR omits passed: %d %s\", code, out)\n    50\t\t}\n    51\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go | sed -n '545,590p;1180,1235p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go | sed -n '110,140p;4010,4105p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go | sed -n '165,195p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go | sed -n '545,590p;1180,1235p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go | sed -n '110,140p;4010,4105p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go | sed -n '165,195p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tpackage pose\n     2\t\n     3\t// Accepted limits (spec pose-review-declared-threat-model): a spec declares\n     4\t// the residual limits of a guarantee it makes, each with a stable id and why\n     5\t// it is accepted. The review plan seals them; the brief lists them; a\n     6\t// reviewer classifies a finding that falls inside one as within that limit,\n     7\t// or disputes the limit as a finding of its own. A declared limit never\n     8\t// hides a defect inside the declared scope: it is visible in the bundle, the\n     9\t// brief and the attestation.\n    10\t\n    11\timport (\n    12\t\t\"regexp\"\n    13\t\t\"strings\"\n    14\t)\n    15\t\n    16\t// ReviewAcceptedLimit is one declared residual limit.\n    17\ttype ReviewAcceptedLimit struct {\n    18\t\tID   string `json:\"id\"`\n    19\t\tText string `json:\"text\"`\n    20\t\t// Spec names the spec that declared the limit when the scope holds more\n    21\t\t// than one; the id is then qualified as <spec>#L<N> (review round 1, N1).\n    22\t\tSpec string `json:\"spec,omitempty\"`\n    23\t}\n    24\t\n    25\tvar acceptedLimitRE = regexp.MustCompile(`^-\\s+(L[1-9][0-9]*):\\s+(.+)$`)\n    26\t\n    27\t// acceptedLimitReasonRE requires a reason after the marker, not the marker\n    28\t// alone (review round 1, N2).\n    29\tvar acceptedLimitReasonRE = regexp.MustCompile(`(?i)(accepted because|aceito porque)\\s+\\S{2,}`)\n    30\t\n    31\t// ParseAcceptedLimits reads the `### Accepted limits` section of a spec body.\n    32\t// It returns the limits and the problems that keep the section from being\n    33\t// read as written: a bullet that is not `- L<N>: ...`, a repeated id, or a\n    34\t// limit that does not say why it is accepted (\"Accepted because ...\" or\n    35\t// \"Aceito porque ...\").\n    36\tfunc ParseAcceptedLimits(body string) ([]ReviewAcceptedLimit, []string) {\n    37\t\tvar limits []ReviewAcceptedLimit\n    38\t\tvar problems []string\n    39\t\tin := false\n    40\t\tseen := map[string]bool{}\n    41\t\tfor _, line := range strings.Split(body, \"\\n\") {\n    42\t\t\ttrimmed := strings.TrimSpace(line)\n    43\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(trimmed, \"#\") {\n    44\t\t\t\tin = strings.EqualFold(strings.TrimSpace(strings.TrimLeft(trimmed, \"#\")), \"Accepted limits\") || strings.EqualFold(strings.TrimSpace(strings.TrimLeft(trimmed, \"#\")), \"Limites aceitos\")\n    45\t\t\t\tcontinue\n    46\t\t\t}\n    47\t\t\tif !in || !strings.HasPrefix(trimmed, \"- \") {\n    48\t\t\t\tcontinue\n    49\t\t\t}\n    50\t\t\tm := acceptedLimitRE.FindStringSubmatch(trimmed)\n    51\t\t\tif m == nil {\n    52\t\t\t\tproblems = append(problems, \"accepted limit \"+quoteLedgerText(trimmed)+\" is not written as '- L<N>: <assumption>. Accepted because <reason>.'\")\n    53\t\t\t\tcontinue\n    54\t\t\t}\n    55\t\t\tif seen[m[1]] {\n    56\t\t\t\tproblems = append(problems, \"accepted limit \"+m[1]+\" is declared twice\")\n    57\t\t\t\tcontinue\n    58\t\t\t}\n    59\t\t\tseen[m[1]] = true\n    60\t\t\tif !acceptedLimitReasonRE.MatchString(m[2]) {\n    61\t\t\t\tproblems = append(problems, \"accepted limit \"+m[1]+\" does not say why it is accepted ('Accepted because ...')\")\n    62\t\t\t}\n    63\t\t\tlimits = append(limits, ReviewAcceptedLimit{ID: m[1], Text: strings.TrimSpace(m[2])})\n    64\t\t}\n    65\t\treturn limits, problems\n    66\t}\n    67\t\n    68\t// acceptedLimitsOf collects the limits the scope's specs declare.\n    69\tfunc (s Store) acceptedLimitsOf(scope ScopeRef) []ReviewAcceptedLimit {\n    70\t\tspecs, err := s.reviewScopeSpecs(scope)\n    71\t\tif err != nil {\n    72\t\t\treturn nil\n    73\t\t}\n    74\t\treturn acceptedLimitsOfSpecs(specs)\n    75\t}\n    76\t\n    77\t// acceptedLimitsOfSpecs collects the limits specs declare, qualifying each id\n    78\t// by its spec when there is more than one spec.\n    79\tfunc acceptedLimitsOfSpecs(specs []Spec) []ReviewAcceptedLimit {\n    80\t\tvar out []ReviewAcceptedLimit\n    81\t\tfor _, spec := range specs {\n    82\t\t\tlimits, _ := ParseAcceptedLimits(spec.Body)\n    83\t\t\tfor _, l := range limits {\n    84\t\t\t\t// Ids are spec-local: across specs each is qualified by its spec,\n    85\t\t\t\t// so a finding names exactly one sealed limit.\n    86\t\t\t\tif len(specs) > 1 {\n    87\t\t\t\t\tl.ID, l.Spec = spec.Slug+\"#\"+l.ID, spec.Slug\n    88\t\t\t\t}\n    89\t\t\t\tout = append(out, l)\n    90\t\t\t}\n    91\t\t}\n    92\t\treturn out\n    93\t}\n    94\t\n    95\t// sealedAcceptedLimit reports whether the bundle sealed limit id.\n    96\tfunc sealedAcceptedLimit(bundle ReviewBundle, id string) bool {\n    97\t\tfor _, l := range bundle.Payload.Plan.AcceptedLimits {\n    98\t\t\tif l.ID == id {\n    99\t\t\t\treturn true\n   100\t\t\t}\n   101\t\t}\n   102\t\treturn false\n   103\t}\n   545\t\t\t\tfield(\"spec.adjudications\", strconv.Itoa(len(adjudications)))\n   546\t\t\t\tfield(\"spec.adjudications.failures\", strconv.Itoa(adjudicationFailures))\n   547\t\t\t}\n   548\t\t}\n   549\t\tif readyCheck {\n   550\t\t\tfailures := 0\n   551\t\t\tfor _, name := range []string{\"Intent\", \"Requirements\", \"Technical Plan\"} {\n   552\t\t\t\tlines, ok := sections[name]\n   553\t\t\t\tif !ok || classifySection(lines) != \"filled\" {\n   554\t\t\t\t\tlint.finding(cliout.StateError, \"dor\", fmt.Sprintf(cliText(locale, \"DoR: section %s is missing, empty, or skeletal\", \"DoR: seção %s ausente/vazia/esquelética\"), name))\n   555\t\t\t\t\tfailures++\n   556\t\t\t\t}\n   557\t\t\t}\n   558\t\t\tif len(parseRequirementIDs(sections[\"Requirements\"])) == 0 {\n   559\t\t\t\tlint.finding(cliout.StateError, \"dor\", cliText(locale, \"DoR: no acceptance criterion has a stable ID (use '- R<N>: ...' bullets in Requirements)\", \"DoR: nenhum acceptance criterion com ID estável (use bullets '- R<N>: ...' em Requirements)\"))\n   560\t\t\t\tfailures++\n   561\t\t\t}\n   562\t\t\tfor _, ref := range lintParseDependsOn(frontmatter[\"depends_on\"]) {\n   563\t\t\t\tif _, err := posepkg.ParseArtifactRef(ref); err == nil {\n   564\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   565\t\t\t\t}\n   566\t\t\t\tlint.finding(cliout.StateError, \"dor\", fmt.Sprintf(cliText(locale, \"DoR: invalid depends_on reference: '%s'\", \"DoR: ref inválida em depends_on: '%s'\"), ref))\n   567\t\t\t\tfailures++\n   568\t\t\t}\n   569\t\t\t// Accepted limits (spec pose-review-declared-threat-model R4): each\n   570\t\t\t// says why it is accepted, and an ADR that names the spec names each\n   571\t\t\t// limit, so the decision record carries what the review will treat as\n   572\t\t\t// out of scope.\n   573\t\t\tlimits, limitProblems := posepkg.ParseAcceptedLimits(text)\n   574\t\t\tfor _, problem := range limitProblems {\n   575\t\t\t\tlint.finding(cliout.StateError, \"dor\", \"DoR: \"+problem)\n   576\t\t\t\tfailures++\n   577\t\t\t}\n   578\t\t\tif len(limits) > 0 {\n   579\t\t\t\tfor _, missing := range acceptedLimitsMissingFromADRs(lintProjectRoot(specPath), slug, limits) {\n   580\t\t\t\t\tlint.finding(cliout.StateError, \"dor\", missing)\n   581\t\t\t\t\tfailures++\n   582\t\t\t\t}\n   583\t\t\t}\n   584\t\t\temitDesignBasis()\n   585\t\t\tfailures += designFailures + lineageFailures\n   586\t\t\tready := \"true\"\n   587\t\t\tif failures > 0 {\n   588\t\t\t\tready = \"false\"\n   589\t\t\t}\n   590\t\t\tfield(\"spec.ready\", ready)\n  1180\t\t\tif n == name {\n  1181\t\t\t\treturn true\n  1182\t\t\t}\n  1183\t\t}\n  1184\t\treturn false\n  1185\t}\n  1186\t\n  1187\t// acceptedLimitsMissingFromADRs names each declared limit an ADR that cites\n  1188\t// the spec does not mention. With no ADR citing the spec nothing is required.\n  1189\tfunc acceptedLimitsMissingFromADRs(root, slug string, limits []posepkg.ReviewAcceptedLimit) []string {\n  1190\t\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(filepath.Join(root, \".pose\", \"adr\"))\n  1191\t\tif err != nil {\n  1192\t\t\treturn nil\n  1193\t\t}\n  1194\t\tvar citing []string\n  1195\t\tfor _, e := range entries {\n  1196\t\t\tif e.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(e.Name(), \".md\") {\n  1197\t\t\t\tcontinue\n  1198\t\t\t}\n  1199\t\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".pose\", \"adr\", e.Name()))\n  1200\t\t\tif err != nil || !strings.Contains(string(raw), slug) {\n  1201\t\t\t\tcontinue\n  1202\t\t\t}\n  1203\t\t\tciting = append(citing, string(raw))\n  1204\t\t}\n  1205\t\tif len(citing) == 0 {\n  1206\t\t\treturn nil\n  1207\t\t}\n  1208\t\tvar missing []string\n  1209\t\tfor _, l := range limits {\n  1210\t\t\tfound := false\n  1211\t\t\t// The id as a word: L10 does not name L1 (review round 1, N3).\n  1212\t\t\tnamed := regexp.MustCompile(`\\b` + regexp.QuoteMeta(l.ID) + `\\b`)\n  1213\t\t\tfor _, adr := range citing {\n  1214\t\t\t\tfound = found || named.MatchString(adr)\n  1215\t\t\t}\n  1216\t\t\tif !found {\n  1217\t\t\t\tmissing = append(missing, \"DoR: accepted limit \"+l.ID+\" is not named by the ADR that cites \"+slug)\n  1218\t\t\t}\n  1219\t\t}\n  1220\t\treturn missing\n  1221\t}\n   110\t\t// Attribution narrows each path to what this scope's own commits changed\n   111\t\t// (see ReviewBundlePathAttribution). It is not implementation identity, so\n   112\t\t// the implementation, patch and tree digests leave it out; it is sealed with\n   113\t\t// the rest of the payload. Absent on bundles sealed before it existed, and\n   114\t\t// whenever Git could not answer: the structural assessment then compares\n   115\t\t// Base and Head.\n   116\t\tAttribution []ReviewBundlePathAttribution `json:\"attribution,omitempty\"`\n   117\t}\n   118\t\n   119\ttype ReviewBundlePlan struct {\n   120\t\tDelegatedRunProofRequired bool     `json:\"delegated_run_proof_required,omitempty\"`\n   121\t\tLimitations               []string `json:\"limitations,omitempty\"`\n   122\t\t// AcceptedLimits seals the residual limits the scope's spec declares, so\n   123\t\t// the brief and the conclusion read them from the bundle (spec\n   124\t\t// pose-review-declared-threat-model). Omitted when none, so every other\n   125\t\t// bundle keeps its digest.\n   126\t\tAcceptedLimits []ReviewAcceptedLimit `json:\"accepted_limits,omitempty\"`\n   127\t\tPlanDigest     string                `json:\"plan_digest\"`\n   128\t\tIndependence   string                `json:\"independence\"`\n   129\t\tComponents     []ReviewPlanComponent `json:\"components\"`\n   130\t\tCriteria       []ReviewPlanCriterion `json:\"criteria\"`\n   131\t\tTools          []ReviewPlanTool      `json:\"tools\"`\n   132\t\t// SelectedProfiles records which components each profile was selected for.\n   133\t\t// A criterion names the profiles it came from, and without this mapping the\n   134\t\t// sealed subject cannot say which components that criterion answers for —\n   135\t\t// so evidence could only be matched by reference and class, never by where\n   136\t\t// it came from. Re-reading it from the current policy at verification time\n   137\t\t// would judge an immutable bundle by today's selection, which is the whole\n   138\t\t// thing sealing exists to prevent.\n   139\t\tSelectedProfiles []ReviewPlanProfile `json:\"selected_profiles,omitempty\"`\n   140\t\t// CloseoutReview seals the closeout-review@1 decision an aggregate scope\n  4010\t\t\tif !seen[id] {\n  4011\t\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"missing criterion \"+id)\n  4012\t\t\t}\n  4013\t\t}\n  4014\t\t// Every criterion dispensed with is not a review of anything. The engine\n  4015\t\t// cannot judge whether one dispensation is honest, but it can refuse the\n  4016\t\t// degenerate case, where the attestation states that nothing the plan asked\n  4017\t\t// about applies to the change it approves.\n  4018\t\t//\n  4019\t\t// Bounded to a scope that carries a delivery target, because the other case\n  4020\t\t// is already modelled and already honest: a documentation-only spec collects\n  4021\t\t// no validation evidence by design, and recording every criterion\n  4022\t\t// not-applicable — naming what is missing — is the answer the engine itself\n  4023\t\t// prepares for it. Refusing that would break the distinction this contract\n  4024\t\t// depends on rather than reinforce it.\n  4025\t\tif judgmentGoverned && hasDeliveryTarget && len(required) > 0 && notApplicable == len(required) && len(att.Criteria) == len(required) {\n  4026\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"every required criterion is not-applicable; a scope where the whole plan is inapplicable is not reviewed by it\")\n  4027\t\t}\n  4028\t\treuseBlockers, _ := s.evaluateReviewReuse(bundle, att, bundle.Payload.SealedGates().AllowCriterionReuse)\n  4029\t\tblockers = append(blockers, reuseBlockers...)\n  4030\t\tsealedEvidence := map[string]ReviewBundleEvidence{}\n  4031\t\tfor _, ev := range bundle.Payload.Evidence {\n  4032\t\t\tsealedEvidence[ev.EvidenceClass+\":\"+ev.ID] = ev\n  4033\t\t}\n  4034\t\tif skipEvidenceSupport {\n  4035\t\t\tsealedEvidence = nil\n  4036\t\t}\n  4037\t\ttoolWarnings, toolBlockers := evaluateReviewToolCoverageIn(s.fsys(), s.Root, bundle.Payload.Plan.Tools, att.Tools, sealedEvidence, hasDeliveryTarget)\n  4038\t\t_ = toolWarnings\n  4039\t\tblockers = append(blockers, toolBlockers...)\n  4040\t\tblockers = append(blockers, reviewFindingDecisionBlockers(bundle, att)...)\n  4041\t\treturn blockers\n  4042\t}\n  4043\t\n  4044\t// The same finding and decision gate protects fresh and reused approvals.\n  4045\tfunc reviewFindingDecisionBlockers(bundle ReviewBundle, att ReviewAttestation) []string {\n  4046\t\tblockers := []string{}\n  4047\t\t// The finding contract, which this path did not have. It accepted a\n  4048\t\t// `critical` risk with no owner, no rationale and no review date; a\n  4049\t\t// disposition the engine does not know; and a finding with neither severity\n  4050\t\t// nor action — all three with no blocker at all, while the legacy attempt\n  4051\t\t// path refused every one of them. A project that adopted review bundles\n  4052\t\t// silently lost the gate (spec\n  4053\t\t// pose-bundle-findings-take-the-contract-the-legacy-path-had).\n  4054\t\t//\n  4055\t\t// Only the accepted-risk severities and the reservations flag come from the\n  4056\t\t// sealed gates. The rest is not configuration: a finding without a severity\n  4057\t\t// is incomplete under any policy.\n  4058\t\tallowedRisk := map[string]bool{}\n  4059\t\tfor _, severity := range bundle.Payload.SealedGates().AcceptedRiskSeverities {\n  4060\t\t\tallowedRisk[severity] = true\n  4061\t\t}\n  4062\t\tseenFindings := map[string]bool{}\n  4063\t\tfor _, finding := range att.Findings {\n  4064\t\t\tif seenFindings[finding.ID] {\n  4065\t\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"duplicate finding \"+finding.ID)\n  4066\t\t\t}\n  4067\t\t\tseenFindings[finding.ID] = true\n  4068\t\t\tif finding.Severity == \"\" || finding.Action == \"\" {\n  4069\t\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"finding \"+finding.ID+\" lacks severity or action\")\n  4070\t\t\t}\n  4071\t\t\tswitch finding.Disposition {\n  4072\t\t\tcase \"resolved\":\n  4073\t\t\tcase \"accepted-risk\", \"wont-fix\":\n  4074\t\t\t\t// Leaving a finding unresolved accepts its risk regardless of the\n  4075\t\t\t\t// disposition's spelling. Use the policy frozen into this bundle.\n  4076\t\t\t\tif !allowedRisk[finding.Severity] || finding.Owner == \"\" || finding.Rationale == \"\" || finding.ReviewBy == \"\" {\n  4077\t\t\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"finding \"+finding.ID+\" has unapproved or incomplete accepted risk\")\n  4078\t\t\t\t}\n  4079\t\t\tcase \"within-limit\":\n  4080\t\t\t\t// Inside a limit the spec declared and the bundle sealed, whatever\n  4081\t\t\t\t// its severity; a limit the bundle did not seal accepts nothing\n  4082\t\t\t\t// (spec pose-review-declared-threat-model R3).\n  4083\t\t\t\tif !sealedAcceptedLimit(bundle, finding.Limit) {\n  4084\t\t\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"finding \"+finding.ID+\" names accepted limit \"+firstNonempty(finding.Limit, \"(none)\")+\", which this bundle did not seal\")\n  4085\t\t\t\t} else if finding.Rationale == \"\" {\n  4086\t\t\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"finding \"+finding.ID+\" is within limit \"+finding.Limit+\" without saying why\")\n  4087\t\t\t\t}\n  4088\t\t\tcase \"open\", \"changes-requested\":\n  4089\t\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"finding \"+finding.ID+\" is \"+finding.Disposition)\n  4090\t\t\tdefault:\n  4091\t\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"finding \"+finding.ID+\" has invalid disposition\")\n  4092\t\t\t}\n  4093\t\t}\n  4094\t\tif att.Decision != \"approved\" && !(att.Decision == \"approved-with-reservations\" && bundle.Payload.SealedGates().AllowApprovedWithReservations) {\n  4095\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"review decision does not permit closeout: \"+att.Decision)\n  4096\t\t}\n  4097\t\treturn blockers\n  4098\t}\n  4099\t\n  4100\tfunc (s Store) verifyStoredReviewAttestationSignature(att ReviewAttestation) error {\n  4101\t\tif att.Envelope == nil {\n  4102\t\t\t// Recorded before signing was required, and sealed unchanged into a\n  4103\t\t\t// trusted legacy ledger (spec pose-signed-legacy-attestation-ledger).\n  4104\t\t\tif s.legacyLedgerCovers(att) {\n  4105\t\t\t\treturn nil\n   165\t\tfor _, t := range draft.Tools {\n   166\t\t\ttools = append(tools, ReviewToolDisposition{ID: t.ID, Component: t.Component, Disposition: t.Disposition, Evidence: t.Evidence, Rationale: t.Rationale})\n   167\t\t}\n   168\t\tatt.Tools = ReviewToolDefaults(bundle.Payload.Plan.Tools, tools)\n   169\t\tfor _, f := range draft.Findings {\n   170\t\t\tfinding := ReviewFinding{ID: f.ID, Severity: f.Severity, Evidence: findingEvidence(f), Action: f.Action, Disposition: \"open\"}\n   171\t\t\tif f.Action == \"\" {\n   172\t\t\t\tfinding.Action = f.Summary\n   173\t\t\t}\n   174\t\t\t// A follow-up the reviewer gave an action, an owner and a review date\n   175\t\t\t// is a risk the reviewer accepted; anything else stays open and blocks\n   176\t\t\t// an approval. The engine never writes the action for the reviewer\n   177\t\t\t// (review round 1, B3).\n   178\t\t\tif f.Disposition == \"follow-up\" && f.Action != \"\" && f.Owner != \"\" && f.ReviewBy != \"\" {\n   179\t\t\t\tfinding.Disposition, finding.Owner, finding.ReviewBy, finding.Rationale = \"accepted-risk\", f.Owner, f.ReviewBy, f.Summary\n   180\t\t\t}\n   181\t\t\t// A follow-up the reviewer classified inside a declared accepted\n   182\t\t\t// limit is recorded as such, naming the limit (spec\n   183\t\t\t// pose-review-declared-threat-model R3).\n   184\t\t\tif f.Disposition == \"follow-up\" && f.Limit != \"\" {\n   185\t\t\t\tfinding.Disposition, finding.Limit, finding.Rationale, finding.Owner, finding.ReviewBy = \"within-limit\", f.Limit, f.Summary, f.Owner, f.ReviewBy\n   186\t\t\t}\n   187\t\t\tatt.Findings = append(att.Findings, finding)\n   188\t\t}\n   189\t\tfor ref := range evidence {\n   190\t\t\tatt.EvidenceRefs = append(att.EvidenceRefs, ref)\n   191\t\t}\n   192\t\tsort.Strings(att.EvidenceRefs)\n   193\t\tatt.Run = &ReviewRunReference{RunID: run.RunID}\n   194\t\treturn att\n   195\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
