e995ae38da18725206bf5c93e018cf2b5cfc reason:attributed implementation path in the immutable change set\\ninclude.subject=pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go class:implementation digest:sha256:fb68205937b56f47b322587dad6fefccd268f793ab87f405940ab78ae0d4eadb reason:attributed implementation path in the immutable change set\\ninclude.subject=pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go class:implementation digest:sha256:760642e4f6aa5c76b0b397011dd6a28ec9e18e0f66c6d31e5ed2979d38e78947 reason:attributed implementation path in the immutable change set\\ninclude.subject=pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go class:implementation digest:sha256:a45190d66aaedaed5a869aa250a228fc13fe0176fdd8a2b5e851fa714bf20999 reason:attributed implementation path in the immutable change set\\ninclude.subject=pose-mcp/internal/pose/testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json class:implementation digest:sha256:bff7cef69d15cfc10130d0ce9fe046ac31dad50500ba0c40ba2ed188b47d36f7 reason:attributed implementation path in the immutable change set\\ninclude.subject=pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md class:implementation digest:sha256:8e8340b5500175f73ab8ed68369af27345f8a4f677641c474ab826c86930b265 reason:attributed implementation path in the immutable change set\\ninclude.subject=pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md class:implementation digest:sha256:80718c8a6ddb3fe12fd7d606e0455a2539cfab16b6f37ae4567a5fe4be675410 reason:attributed implementation path in the immutable change set\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-d1680df442b23d12.transcript:80:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_42\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/usr/bin/bash -lc \\\"cat <<'POSE_FINAL_MESSAGE' | \\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" review draft-check --draft -\\ndecision: changes-requested\\n\\n## Review\\n\\nReviewed the sealed request bundle `rvb-8c5b48b85bb59245` (`sha256:8c5b48b85bb5924542b10d6612fd8200890d9d7c346be8acf9aca5d22872a784`). The independent code review found three defects in accepted-limit parsing and identity.\\n\\n## Criterion results\\n\\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| assumption-integrity | passed | `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\\n| backend-concurrency | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration` |\\n| backend-contracts | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\\n| backend-input-errors | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract` |\\n| backend-observability | passed | `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\\n| compatibility | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\\n| correctness | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\\n| design-causality | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n| documentation | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n| operability | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\\n| requirements | failed (N1, N2, N3) | R1–R4; findings below |\\n| scope | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n| security | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\\n| solution-proportionality | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n- **N1 — medium, blocker:** [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) appends limits from every spec in a roadmap or milestone without preserving the source spec or rejecting duplicate IDs. Since each spec can independently use `L1` and findings store only that ID, the brief and attestation cannot unambiguously identify which sealed limit was used.\\n- **N2 — medium, blocker:** [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) accepts the phrase `Accepted because` with no explanation after it. A spec can therefore pass `lint-spec --ready-check` and seal an unjustified limit, contrary to R4.\\n- **N3 — low, blocker:** [lintspec.go:1212](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:1212) uses substring matching for ADR IDs, so an ADR containing `L10` satisfies a required reference to `L1`.\\n\\n## Limit judgment and review boundary\\n\\nL1 is justified as a disclosed human-review risk for a single-spec bundle: the brief presents the limit text as data, asks for a reason why a finding falls within it, and requires a dispute to be a blocking finding. L2 is justified by the plan digest and `omitempty` fields, which keep later edits in a new bundle and preserve prior empty-limit digests. For one-spec reviews the gate rejects unsealed IDs and empty finding rationales; whether a natural-language finding truly matches a limit remains reviewer judgment under D1. N1 breaks unambiguous attribution when multiple specs are reviewed together.\\n\\n## Validation and tool results\\n\\nThe focused command `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '\\\"'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud'\\\"'` passed. `surface-check` passed with one target and zero findings. Both strict `validate` invocations finished but failed because the read-only sandbox prevented Go from creating work directories and cache files; the sealed bundle contains passing `build:pose-mcp/go/build` and `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` evidence. The artifact-check command exited 0 but resolved change set `cs-6010196c7421` (head `573858...`) instead of this brief'\\\"'s \\\"'`cs-2f8efba58158`; its 19-claim/30-observation repository warnings are not treated as defects in the sealed subject. The tech-debt scan was incomplete due two invalid specs and one uncovered repository marker; no marker was found in the changed accepted-limit implementation. The recurrence check found no flagged keys.\\n\\nRules applied: `.pose/workflows/review.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md`, `.pose/rules/backend-go.md` and `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`. No relevant prior handoff was found. `review-check` and `closeout-check` remain deferred until an attestation exists; no attestation or repository edits were made.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 71,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Composite roadmap or milestone plans append limits from multiple specs without preserving the source spec or checking ID collisions. Since IDs are spec-local L<N> values and findings record only limit, duplicate L1 entries make the brief and attestation ambiguous; the gate accepts either one, so R3 cannot reliably identify which limit classified the finding.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 54,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The ready-check treats the substring '\\\"'Accepted because' as a reason even when it ends the entry (for example, '- L1: assumption. Accepted because'). That unjustified limit is parsed and sealed, so R4's justification gate has a false pass.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N3\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"low\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"blocker\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"line\\\\\\\": 1212,\\n      \\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ADR coverage uses substring matching for limit IDs. An ADR mentioning L10 therefore satisfies the required reference to L1, allowing an ADR that omits L1 to pass ready-check.\\\\\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\\\\\"criteria\\\\\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assumption-integrity\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I examined the two sealed limits and their consumers. L1's dependence on an independent reviewer inspecting the displayed text is explicit and accepted for a single-spec review; L2 is supported by the limit's inclusion in the plan digest and optional bundle field. Semantic fit remains reviewer judgment, and N1 identifies the composite-scope ambiguity.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-concurrency\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-contracts\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Composite review findings cannot unambiguously name one of two same-ID limits.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-input-errors\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N2\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A limit with no text after the acceptance phrase passes validation.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-integration-impact\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-observability\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"compatibility\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The new limit identity contract is ambiguous when a plan contains multiple specs.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"correctness\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N2\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The ready-check accepts an unjustified limit; N1 also affects composite reviews.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"design-causality\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"D1 addresses non-convergence by recording an explicit reviewer classification; D2 binds the limits into the plan and bundle digests. The inspected implementation follows that design, with the specific defects reported separately. The structural assessment observed no deltas.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"documentation\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I compared the English and Portuguese manuals and their scaffold copies with runtime behavior: they describe the new section, sealed plan/bundle, review-brief/11 classification, and ready-check.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"operability\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N2\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The ready-check reports unjustified limits in normal cases but gives a false pass when the reason phrase has no explanation.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"requirements\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"R3 is ambiguous for composite scopes (N1); R4 also has false passes for empty reasons and partial ADR ID matches (N2, N3).\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The inspected prepared subject contained the 18 implementation/documentation paths named by the spec artifacts, and the design assessment observed no structural delta.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"security\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A composite-scope finding can be accepted against an ambiguous same-ID limit, weakening the integrity of the approval classification.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"solution-proportionality\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The optional sealed field, versioned brief and typed finding field are a small sufficient design for preserving review-time assumptions; the digest omission preserves existing records. The reported defects are validation gaps, not speculative architecture.\\\\\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\\\\\"tools\\\\\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"artifact-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The command exited 0. It selected cs-6010196c7421, not the brief's cs-2f8efba58158, and reported 19 claims versus 30 observations with unrelated repository-wide orphan warnings; those warnings are not treated as scoped findings.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-design\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran the recommended assessment; it observed the subject and reported no structural deltas.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-discover\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"component\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran without persistence and confirmed the pose-mcp component.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-integrate\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran the assessment. It reported three unobserved HTTP consumers (/admin/refresh, /healthz, /mcp), outside the changed CLI/review-limit boundary.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-tech-debt\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"failed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The scan was incomplete: two invalid specs were unread and one debt item was uncovered. No marker was found in the changed accepted-limit implementation.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"closeout-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"deferred\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The brief says closeout-check requires completion of the review; no attestation is recorded in this run.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"review-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"deferred\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The brief says review-check requires completion of the review; no attestation is recorded in this run.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"surface-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The required surface check completed with one target, 236 results and zero findings.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"validate\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The required rerun could not create Go work/cache files in the read-only sandbox; the sealed bundle's pose-mcp build evidence is pass.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"validate\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"component\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The required module rerun was blocked by the read-only Go work/cache paths; the sealed full pose-mcp unit result is pass, and the focused review tests also passed.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"suggest-review\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"component\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran and selected backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\\\\\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\\"'```\\nPOSE_FINAL_MESSAGE'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-d1680df442b23d12.transcript:81:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_42\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/usr/bin/bash -lc \\\"cat <<'POSE_FINAL_MESSAGE' | \\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" review draft-check --draft -\\ndecision: changes-requested\\n\\n## Review\\n\\nReviewed the sealed request bundle `rvb-8c5b48b85bb59245` (`sha256:8c5b48b85bb5924542b10d6612fd8200890d9d7c346be8acf9aca5d22872a784`). The independent code review found three defects in accepted-limit parsing and identity.\\n\\n## Criterion results\\n\\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| assumption-integrity | passed | `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\\n| backend-concurrency | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration` |\\n| backend-contracts | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\\n| backend-input-errors | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract` |\\n| backend-observability | passed | `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\\n| compatibility | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\\n| correctness | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\\n| design-causality | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n| documentation | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n| operability | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\\n| requirements | failed (N1, N2, N3) | R1–R4; findings below |\\n| scope | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n| security | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\\n| solution-proportionality | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n- **N1 — medium, blocker:** [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) appends limits from every spec in a roadmap or milestone without preserving the source spec or rejecting duplicate IDs. Since each spec can independently use `L1` and findings store only that ID, the brief and attestation cannot unambiguously identify which sealed limit was used.\\n- **N2 — medium, blocker:** [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) accepts the phrase `Accepted because` with no explanation after it. A spec can therefore pass `lint-spec --ready-check` and seal an unjustified limit, contrary to R4.\\n- **N3 — low, blocker:** [lintspec.go:1212](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:1212) uses substring matching for ADR IDs, so an ADR containing `L10` satisfies a required reference to `L1`.\\n\\n## Limit judgment and review boundary\\n\\nL1 is justified as a disclosed human-review risk for a single-spec bundle: the brief presents the limit text as data, asks for a reason why a finding falls within it, and requires a dispute to be a blocking finding. L2 is justified by the plan digest and `omitempty` fields, which keep later edits in a new bundle and preserve prior empty-limit digests. For one-spec reviews the gate rejects unsealed IDs and empty finding rationales; whether a natural-language finding truly matches a limit remains reviewer judgment under D1. N1 breaks unambiguous attribution when multiple specs are reviewed together.\\n\\n## Validation and tool results\\n\\nThe focused command `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '\\\"'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud'\\\"'` passed. `surface-check` passed with one target and zero findings. Both strict `validate` invocations finished but failed because the read-only sandbox prevented Go from creating work directories and cache files; the sealed bundle contains passing `build:pose-mcp/go/build` and `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` evidence. The artifact-check command exited 0 but resolved change set `cs-6010196c7421` (head `573858...`) instead of this brief'\\\"'s \\\"'`cs-2f8efba58158`; its 19-claim/30-observation repository warnings are not treated as defects in the sealed subject. The tech-debt scan was incomplete due two invalid specs and one uncovered repository marker; no marker was found in the changed accepted-limit implementation. The recurrence check found no flagged keys.\\n\\nRules applied: `.pose/workflows/review.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md`, `.pose/rules/backend-go.md` and `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`. No relevant prior handoff was found. `review-check` and `closeout-check` remain deferred until an attestation exists; no attestation or repository edits were made.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 71,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Composite roadmap or milestone plans append limits from multiple specs without preserving the source spec or checking ID collisions. Since IDs are spec-local L<N> values and findings record only limit, duplicate L1 entries make the brief and attestation ambiguous; the gate accepts either one, so R3 cannot reliably identify which limit classified the finding.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 54,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The ready-check treats the substring '\\\"'Accepted because' as a reason even when it ends the entry (for example, '- L1: assumption. Accepted because'). That unjustified limit is parsed and sealed, so R4's justification gate has a false pass.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N3\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"low\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"blocker\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"line\\\\\\\": 1212,\\n      \\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ADR coverage uses substring matching for limit IDs. An ADR mentioning L10 therefore satisfies the required reference to L1, allowing an ADR that omits L1 to pass ready-check.\\\\\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\\\\\"criteria\\\\\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assumption-integrity\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I examined the two sealed limits and their consumers. L1's dependence on an independent reviewer inspecting the displayed text is explicit and accepted for a single-spec review; L2 is supported by the limit's inclusion in the plan digest and optional bundle field. Semantic fit remains reviewer judgment, and N1 identifies the composite-scope ambiguity.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-concurrency\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-contracts\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Composite review findings cannot unambiguously name one of two same-ID limits.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-input-errors\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N2\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A limit with no text after the acceptance phrase passes validation.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-integration-impact\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-observability\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"compatibility\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The new limit identity contract is ambiguous when a plan contains multiple specs.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"correctness\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N2\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The ready-check accepts an unjustified limit; N1 also affects composite reviews.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"design-causality\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"D1 addresses non-convergence by recording an explicit reviewer classification; D2 binds the limits into the plan and bundle digests. The inspected implementation follows that design, with the specific defects reported separately. The structural assessment observed no deltas.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"documentation\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I compared the English and Portuguese manuals and their scaffold copies with runtime behavior: they describe the new section, sealed plan/bundle, review-brief/11 classification, and ready-check.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"operability\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N2\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The ready-check reports unjustified limits in normal cases but gives a false pass when the reason phrase has no explanation.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"requirements\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"R3 is ambiguous for composite scopes (N1); R4 also has false passes for empty reasons and partial ADR ID matches (N2, N3).\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The inspected prepared subject contained the 18 implementation/documentation paths named by the spec artifacts, and the design assessment observed no structural delta.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"security\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A composite-scope finding can be accepted against an ambiguous same-ID limit, weakening the integrity of the approval classification.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"solution-proportionality\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The optional sealed field, versioned brief and typed finding field are a small sufficient design for preserving review-time assumptions; the digest omission preserves existing records. The reported defects are validation gaps, not speculative architecture.\\\\\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\\\\\"tools\\\\\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"artifact-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The command exited 0. It selected cs-6010196c7421, not the brief's cs-2f8efba58158, and reported 19 claims versus 30 observations with unrelated repository-wide orphan warnings; those warnings are not treated as scoped findings.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-design\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran the recommended assessment; it observed the subject and reported no structural deltas.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-discover\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"component\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran without persistence and confirmed the pose-mcp component.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-integrate\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran the assessment. It reported three unobserved HTTP consumers (/admin/refresh, /healthz, /mcp), outside the changed CLI/review-limit boundary.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-tech-debt\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"failed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The scan was incomplete: two invalid specs were unread and one debt item was uncovered. No marker was found in the changed accepted-limit implementation.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"closeout-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"deferred\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The brief says closeout-check requires completion of the review; no attestation is recorded in this run.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"review-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"deferred\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The brief says review-check requires completion of the review; no attestation is recorded in this run.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"surface-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The required surface check completed with one target, 236 results and zero findings.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"validate\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The required rerun could not create Go work/cache files in the read-only sandbox; the sealed bundle's pose-mcp build evidence is pass.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"validate\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"component\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The required module rerun was blocked by the read-only Go work/cache paths; the sealed full pose-mcp unit result is pass, and the focused review tests also passed.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"suggest-review\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"component\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran and selected backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\\\\\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\\"'```\\nPOSE_FINAL_MESSAGE'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Draft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-d1680df442b23d12.transcript:91:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_48\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/usr/bin/bash -lc '\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" review-plan spec:pose-review-declared-threat-model --json | rg '\\\"'plan_digest|accepted_limits|scope_digest'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-d1680df442b23d12.transcript:92:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_48\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/usr/bin/bash -lc '\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" review-plan spec:pose-review-declared-threat-model --json | rg '\\\"'plan_digest|accepted_limits|scope_digest'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"  \\\"scope_digest\\\": \\\"sha256:630addfc59bef1f1e89555cac72de734050cb626ba76eeb7ea7b91348b192c0d\\\",\\n  \\\"plan_digest\\\": \\\"sha256:55a60ed8cd30be693ef9e1323b788b3e0c96d59aaff06b402bb5b1de282baaf7\\\",\\n        \\\"artifact:pose-review-declared-threat-model:pose-mcp/internal/cli/accepted_limits_lint_test.go\\\",\\n        \\\"artifact:pose-review-declared-threat-model:pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\\\",\\n        \\\"artifact:pose-review-declared-threat-model:pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits_test.go\\\",\\n        \\\"observed:pose-review-declared-threat-model:pose-mcp/internal/cli/accepted_limits_lint_test.go\\\",\\n        \\\"observed:pose-review-declared-threat-model:pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\\\",\\n        \\\"observed:pose-review-declared-threat-model:pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits_test.go\\\",\\n  \\\"accepted_limits\\\": [\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-d1680df442b23d12.transcript:93:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_49\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/usr/bin/bash -lc \\\"cat <<'POSE_FINAL_MESSAGE' | \\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" review draft-check --draft -\\ndecision: changes-requested\\n\\n## Review\\n\\nReviewed sealed bundle `rvb-8c5b48b85bb59245` (`sha256:8c5b48b85bb5924542b10d6612fd8200890d9d7c346be8acf9aca5d22872a784`). The dispatcher review-plan view returned `sha256:55a60ed8cd30be693ef9e1323b788b3e0c96d59aaff06b402bb5b1de282baaf7`. The independent review found three defects in accepted-limit identity and validation.\\n\\n## Criterion results\\n\\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| assumption-integrity | passed | `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\\n| backend-concurrency | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration` |\\n| backend-contracts | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\\n| backend-input-errors | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract` |\\n| backend-observability | passed | `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\\n| compatibility | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\\n| correctness | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\\n| design-causality | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n| documentation | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n| operability | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\\n| requirements | failed (N1, N2, N3) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71), [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54), [lintspec.go:1212](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:1212) |\\n| scope | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n| security | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\\n| solution-proportionality | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n- **N1 — medium, blocker:** [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) appends limits from every spec in a roadmap or milestone without preserving the source spec or rejecting duplicate IDs. Since each spec can independently use `L1` and findings store only that ID, the brief and attestation cannot unambiguously identify which sealed limit was used.\\n- **N2 — medium, blocker:** [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) accepts the phrase `Accepted because` with no explanation after it. A spec can therefore pass `lint-spec --ready-check` and seal an unjustified limit, contrary to R4.\\n- **N3 — low, blocker:** [lintspec.go:1212](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:1212) uses substring matching for ADR IDs, so an ADR containing `L10` satisfies a required reference to `L1`.\\n\\n## Limit judgment\\n\\nL1 is justified as a disclosed human-review risk for a single-spec bundle: the brief presents limit text as data, asks for a reason why a finding falls within it, and requires a dispute to be a blocking finding. L2 is justified by the plan digest and `omitempty` fields, which preserve empty-limit plan and bundle digests and make later edits require a new bundle. For one-spec reviews the gate rejects unsealed IDs and empty finding rationales. It cannot prove that a natural-language finding actually matches the limit; D1 assigns that judgment to the reviewer, so an honest independent review is part of L1'\\\"'s assumption. N1 is a concrete attribution flaw for composite scopes.\\n\\n## Validation and tool results\\n\\nThe focused command \\\"'`go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '\\\"'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud'\\\"'` passed. `surface-check` passed with one target and zero findings. Both strict `validate` invocations finished but failed because the read-only sandbox prevented Go from creating work directories and cache files; the sealed bundle contains passing `build:pose-mcp/go/build` and `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` evidence. The artifact-check command exited 0 but resolved change set `cs-6010196c7421` (head `573858...`) instead of this brief'\\\"'s \\\"'`cs-2f8efba58158`; its 19-claim/30-observation repository warnings are not treated as defects in the sealed subject. The tech-debt scan was incomplete due two invalid specs and one uncovered repository marker. The recurrence check found no flagged keys.\\n\\nRules applied: `.pose/workflows/review.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md`, `.pose/rules/backend-go.md` and `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`. No relevant prior handoff was found. `review-check` and `closeout-check` remain deferred until an attestation exists; no attestation or repository edits were made.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 71,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Composite roadmap or milestone plans append limits from multiple specs without preserving the source spec or checking ID collisions. Since IDs are spec-local L<N> values and findings record only limit, the brief and attestation cannot unambiguously identify which sealed limit was used; the gate accepts either one, so R3 attribution is ambiguous.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 54,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The ready-check treats the substring '\\\"'Accepted because' as a reason even when it ends the entry (for example, '- L1: assumption. Accepted because'). That unjustified limit is parsed and sealed, so R4's justification gate has a false pass.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N3\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"low\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"blocker\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"line\\\\\\\": 1212,\\n      \\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ADR coverage uses substring matching for limit IDs. An ADR mentioning L10 therefore satisfies the required reference to L1, allowing an ADR that omits L1 to pass ready-check.\\\\\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\\\\\"criteria\\\\\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assumption-integrity\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I examined the two sealed limits and their consumers. L1's dependence on an independent reviewer inspecting the displayed text is explicit and accepted for a single-spec review; L2 is supported by the limit's inclusion in the plan digest and optional bundle field. Semantic fit remains reviewer judgment, and N1 identifies the composite-scope ambiguity.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-concurrency\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-contracts\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Composite review findings cannot unambiguously name one of two same-ID limits.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-input-errors\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N2\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A limit with no text after the acceptance phrase passes validation.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-integration-impact\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-observability\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"compatibility\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The new limit identity contract is ambiguous when a plan contains multiple specs.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"correctness\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N2\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The ready-check accepts an unjustified limit; N1 also affects composite reviews.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"design-causality\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"D1 addresses non-convergence by recording an explicit reviewer classification; D2 binds the limits into the plan and bundle digests. The inspected implementation follows that design, with the specific defects reported separately. The structural assessment observed no deltas.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"documentation\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I compared the English and Portuguese manuals and their scaffold copies with runtime behavior: they describe the new section, sealed plan/bundle, review-brief/11 classification, and ready-check.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"operability\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N2\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The ready-check reports unjustified limits in normal cases but gives a false pass when the reason phrase has no explanation.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"requirements\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"R3 is ambiguous for composite scopes (N1); R4 also has false passes for empty reasons and partial ADR ID matches (N2, N3).\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The inspected prepared subject contained the 18 implementation/documentation paths named by the spec artifacts, and the design assessment observed no structural delta.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"security\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A composite-scope finding can be accepted against an ambiguous same-ID limit, weakening the integrity of the approval classification.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"solution-proportionality\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The optional sealed field, versioned brief and typed finding field are a small sufficient design for preserving review-time assumptions; the digest omission preserves existing records. The reported defects are validation gaps, not speculative architecture.\\\\\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\\\\\"tools\\\\\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"artifact-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The command exited 0. It selected cs-6010196c7421, not the brief's cs-2f8efba58158, and reported 19 claims versus 30 observations with repository-wide orphan warnings; those warnings are not treated as scoped findings.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-design\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran the recommended assessment; it observed the subject and reported no structural deltas.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-discover\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"component\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran without persistence and confirmed the pose-mcp component.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-integrate\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran the assessment. It reported three unobserved HTTP consumers (/admin/refresh, /healthz, /mcp), outside the changed CLI/review-limit boundary.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-tech-debt\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"failed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The scan was incomplete: two invalid specs were unread and one debt item was uncovered. No marker was found in the changed accepted-limit implementation.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"closeout-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"deferred\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The brief says closeout-check requires completion of the review; no attestation is recorded in this run.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"review-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"deferred\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The brief says review-check requires completion of the review; no attestation is recorded in this run.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"surface-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The required surface check completed with one target, 236 results and zero findings.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"validate\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The required rerun could not create Go work/cache files in the read-only sandbox; the sealed bundle's pose-mcp build evidence is pass.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"validate\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"component\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The required module rerun was blocked by the read-only Go work/cache paths; the sealed full pose-mcp unit result is pass, and the focused review tests also passed.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"suggest-review\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"component\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran and selected backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\\\\\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\\"'```\\nPOSE_FINAL_MESSAGE'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-d1680df442b23d12.transcript:94:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_49\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/usr/bin/bash -lc \\\"cat <<'POSE_FINAL_MESSAGE' | \\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" review draft-check --draft -\\ndecision: changes-requested\\n\\n## Review\\n\\nReviewed sealed bundle `rvb-8c5b48b85bb59245` (`sha256:8c5b48b85bb5924542b10d6612fd8200890d9d7c346be8acf9aca5d22872a784`). The dispatcher review-plan view returned `sha256:55a60ed8cd30be693ef9e1323b788b3e0c96d59aaff06b402bb5b1de282baaf7`. The independent review found three defects in accepted-limit identity and validation.\\n\\n## Criterion results\\n\\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| assumption-integrity | passed | `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\\n| backend-concurrency | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration` |\\n| backend-contracts | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\\n| backend-input-errors | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract` |\\n| backend-observability | passed | `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\\n| compatibility | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\\n| correctness | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\\n| design-causality | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n| documentation | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n| operability | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\\n| requirements | failed (N1, N2, N3) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71), [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54), [lintspec.go:1212](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:1212) |\\n| scope | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n| security | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\\n| solution-proportionality | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n- **N1 — medium, blocker:** [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) appends limits from every spec in a roadmap or milestone without preserving the source spec or rejecting duplicate IDs. Since each spec can independently use `L1` and findings store only that ID, the brief and attestation cannot unambiguously identify which sealed limit was used.\\n- **N2 — medium, blocker:** [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) accepts the phrase `Accepted because` with no explanation after it. A spec can therefore pass `lint-spec --ready-check` and seal an unjustified limit, contrary to R4.\\n- **N3 — low, blocker:** [lintspec.go:1212](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:1212) uses substring matching for ADR IDs, so an ADR containing `L10` satisfies a required reference to `L1`.\\n\\n## Limit judgment\\n\\nL1 is justified as a disclosed human-review risk for a single-spec bundle: the brief presents limit text as data, asks for a reason why a finding falls within it, and requires a dispute to be a blocking finding. L2 is justified by the plan digest and `omitempty` fields, which preserve empty-limit plan and bundle digests and make later edits require a new bundle. For one-spec reviews the gate rejects unsealed IDs and empty finding rationales. It cannot prove that a natural-language finding actually matches the limit; D1 assigns that judgment to the reviewer, so an honest independent review is part of L1'\\\"'s assumption. N1 is a concrete attribution flaw for composite scopes.\\n\\n## Validation and tool results\\n\\nThe focused command \\\"'`go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '\\\"'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud'\\\"'` passed. `surface-check` passed with one target and zero findings. Both strict `validate` invocations finished but failed because the read-only sandbox prevented Go from creating work directories and cache files; the sealed bundle contains passing `build:pose-mcp/go/build` and `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` evidence. The artifact-check command exited 0 but resolved change set `cs-6010196c7421` (head `573858...`) instead of this brief'\\\"'s \\\"'`cs-2f8efba58158`; its 19-claim/30-observation repository warnings are not treated as defects in the sealed subject. The tech-debt scan was incomplete due two invalid specs and one uncovered repository marker. The recurrence check found no flagged keys.\\n\\nRules applied: `.pose/workflows/review.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md`, `.pose/rules/backend-go.md` and `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`. No relevant prior handoff was found. `review-check` and `closeout-check` remain deferred until an attestation exists; no attestation or repository edits were made.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 71,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Composite roadmap or milestone plans append limits from multiple specs without preserving the source spec or checking ID collisions. Since IDs are spec-local L<N> values and findings record only limit, the brief and attestation cannot unambiguously identify which sealed limit was used; the gate accepts either one, so R3 attribution is ambiguous.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 54,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The ready-check treats the substring '\\\"'Accepted because' as a reason even when it ends the entry (for example, '- L1: assumption. Accepted because'). That unjustified limit is parsed and sealed, so R4's justification gate has a false pass.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N3\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"low\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"blocker\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"line\\\\\\\": 1212,\\n      \\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ADR coverage uses substring matching for limit IDs. An ADR mentioning L10 therefore satisfies the required reference to L1, allowing an ADR that omits L1 to pass ready-check.\\\\\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\\\\\"criteria\\\\\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assumption-integrity\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I examined the two sealed limits and their consumers. L1's dependence on an independent reviewer inspecting the displayed text is explicit and accepted for a single-spec review; L2 is supported by the limit's inclusion in the plan digest and optional bundle field. Semantic fit remains reviewer judgment, and N1 identifies the composite-scope ambiguity.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-concurrency\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-contracts\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Composite review findings cannot unambiguously name one of two same-ID limits.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-input-errors\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N2\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A limit with no text after the acceptance phrase passes validation.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-integration-impact\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"backend-observability\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"compatibility\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The new limit identity contract is ambiguous when a plan contains multiple specs.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"correctness\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N2\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The ready-check accepts an unjustified limit; N1 also affects composite reviews.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"design-causality\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"D1 addresses non-convergence by recording an explicit reviewer classification; D2 binds the limits into the plan and bundle digests. The inspected implementation follows that design, with the specific defects reported separately. The structural assessment observed no deltas.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"documentation\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I compared the English and Portuguese manuals and their scaffold copies with runtime behavior: they describe the new section, sealed plan/bundle, review-brief/11 classification, and ready-check.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"operability\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N2\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The ready-check reports unjustified limits in normal cases but gives a false pass when the reason phrase has no explanation.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"requirements\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"R3 is ambiguous for composite scopes (N1); R4 also has false passes for empty reasons and partial ADR ID matches (N2, N3).\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The inspected prepared subject contained the 18 implementation/documentation paths named by the spec artifacts, and the design assessment observed no structural delta.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"security\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N1\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A composite-scope finding can be accepted against an ambiguous same-ID limit, weakening the integrity of the approval classification.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"solution-proportionality\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The optional sealed field, versioned brief and typed finding field are a small sufficient design for preserving review-time assumptions; the digest omission preserves existing records. The reported defects are validation gaps, not speculative architecture.\\\\\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\\\\\"tools\\\\\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"artifact-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The command exited 0. It selected cs-6010196c7421, not the brief's cs-2f8efba58158, and reported 19 claims versus 30 observations with repository-wide orphan warnings; those warnings are not treated as scoped findings.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-design\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran the recommended assessment; it observed the subject and reported no structural deltas.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-discover\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"component\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran without persistence and confirmed the pose-mcp component.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-integrate\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran the assessment. It reported three unobserved HTTP consumers (/admin/refresh, /healthz, /mcp), outside the changed CLI/review-limit boundary.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assess-tech-debt\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"failed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The scan was incomplete: two invalid specs were unread and one debt item was uncovered. No marker was found in the changed accepted-limit implementation.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"closeout-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"deferred\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The brief says closeout-check requires completion of the review; no attestation is recorded in this run.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"review-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"deferred\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The brief says review-check requires completion of the review; no attestation is recorded in this run.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"surface-check\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The required surface check completed with one target, 236 results and zero findings.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"validate\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The required rerun could not create Go work/cache files in the read-only sandbox; the sealed bundle's pose-mcp build evidence is pass.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"validate\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"component\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The required module rerun was blocked by the read-only Go work/cache paths; the sealed full pose-mcp unit result is pass, and the focused review tests also passed.\\\\\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"suggest-review\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"component\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"disposition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\\\\\",\\n      \\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ran and selected backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\\\\\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\\"'```\\nPOSE_FINAL_MESSAGE'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Draft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-d1680df442b23d12.transcript:95:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_50\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"decision: changes-requested\\n\\n## Review\\n\\nReviewed sealed bundle `rvb-8c5b48b85bb59245` (`sha256:8c5b48b85bb5924542b10d6612fd8200890d9d7c346be8acf9aca5d22872a784`). The dispatcher review-plan view returned `sha256:55a60ed8cd30be693ef9e1323b788b3e0c96d59aaff06b402bb5b1de282baaf7`. The independent review found three defects in accepted-limit identity and validation.\\n\\n## Criterion results\\n\\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| assumption-integrity | passed | `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\\n| backend-concurrency | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration` |\\n| backend-contracts | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\\n| backend-input-errors | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract` |\\n| backend-observability | passed | `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\\n| compatibility | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\\n| correctness | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\\n| design-causality | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n| documentation | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n| operability | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\\n| requirements | failed (N1, N2, N3) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71), [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54), [lintspec.go:1212](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:1212) |\\n| scope | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n| security | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\\n| solution-proportionality | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n- **N1 — medium, blocker:** [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) appends limits from every spec in a roadmap or milestone without preserving the source spec or rejecting duplicate IDs. Since each spec can independently use `L1` and findings store only that ID, the brief and attestation cannot unambiguously identify which sealed limit was used.\\n\\n- **N2 — medium, blocker:** [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) accepts the phrase `Accepted because` with no explanation after it. A spec can therefore pass `lint-spec --ready-check` and seal an unjustified limit, contrary to R4.\\n\\n- **N3 — low, blocker:** [lintspec.go:1212](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:1212) uses substring matching for ADR IDs, so an ADR containing `L10` satisfies a required reference to `L1`.\\n\\n## Limit judgment\\n\\nL1 is justified as a disclosed human-review risk for a single-spec bundle: the brief presents limit text as data, asks for a reason why a finding falls within it, and requires a dispute to be a blocking finding. L2 is justified by the plan digest and `omitempty` fields, which preserve empty-limit plan and bundle digests and make later edits require a new bundle.\\n\\nFor one-spec reviews, the gate rejects unsealed IDs and empty finding rationales. It cannot prove that a natural-language finding actually matches the limit; D1 assigns that judgment to the reviewer, so an honest independent review is part of L1’s assumption. N1 is a concrete attribution flaw for composite scopes.\\n\\n## Validation and tool results\\n\\nThe focused command `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud'` passed. `surface-check` passed with one target and zero findings. Both strict `validate` invocations finished but failed because the read-only sandbox prevented Go from creating work directories and cache files; the sealed bundle contains passing `build:pose-mcp/go/build` and `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` evidence.\\n\\nThe artifact-check command exited 0 but resolved change set `cs-6010196c7421` (head `573858...`) instead of this brief’s `cs-2f8efba58158`; its 19-claim/30-observation repository warnings are not treated as defects in the sealed subject. The tech-debt scan was incomplete due two invalid specs and one uncovered repository marker. The recurrence check found no flagged keys.\\n\\nRules applied: `.pose/workflows/review.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md`, `.pose/rules/backend-go.md` and `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`. No relevant prior handoff was found. `review-check` and `closeout-check` remain deferred until an attestation exists; no attestation or repository edits were made.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 71,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Composite roadmap or milestone plans append limits from multiple specs without preserving the source spec or checking ID collisions. Since IDs are spec-local L<N> values and findings record only limit, the brief and attestation cannot unambiguously identify which sealed limit was used; the gate accepts either one, so R3 attribution is ambiguous.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 54,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The ready-check treats the substring 'Accepted because' as a reason even when it ends the entry (for example, '- L1: assumption. Accepted because'). That unjustified limit is parsed and sealed, so R4's justification gate has a false pass.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 1212,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"ADR coverage uses substring matching for limit IDs. An ADR mentioning L10 therefore satisfies the required reference to L1, allowing an ADR that omits L1 to pass ready-check.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"I examined the two sealed limits and their consumers. L1's dependence on an independent reviewer inspecting the displayed text is explicit and accepted for a single-spec review; L2 is supported by the limit's inclusion in the plan digest and optional bundle field. Semantic fit remains reviewer judgment, and N1 identifies the composite-scope ambiguity.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Composite review findings cannot unambiguously name one of two same-ID limits.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A limit with no text after the acceptance phrase passes validation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The new limit identity contract is ambiguous when a plan contains multiple specs.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The ready-check accepts an unjustified limit; N1 also affects composite reviews.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses non-convergence by recording an explicit reviewer classification; D2 binds the limits into the plan and bundle digests. The inspected implementation follows that design, with the specific defects reported separately. The structural assessment observed no deltas.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"I compared the English and Portuguese manuals and their scaffold copies with runtime behavior: they describe the new section, sealed plan/bundle, review-brief/11 classification, and ready-check.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The ready-check reports unjustified limits in normal cases but gives a false pass when the reason phrase has no explanation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R3 is ambiguous for composite scopes (N1); R4 also has false passes for empty reasons and partial ADR ID matches (N2, N3).\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The inspected prepared subject contained the 18 implementation/documentation paths named by the spec artifacts, and the design assessment observed no structural delta.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A composite-scope finding can be accepted against an ambiguous same-ID limit, weakening the integrity of the approval classification.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The optional sealed field, versioned brief and typed finding field are a small sufficient design for preserving review-time assumptions; the digest omission preserves existing records. The reported defects are validation gaps, not speculative architecture.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The command exited 0. It selected cs-6010196c7421, not the brief's cs-2f8efba58158, and reported 19 claims versus 30 observations with repository-wide orphan warnings; those warnings are not treated as scoped findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the recommended assessment; it observed the subject and reported no structural deltas.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran without persistence and confirmed the pose-mcp component.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the assessment. It reported three unobserved HTTP consumers (/admin/refresh, /healthz, /mcp), outside the changed CLI/review-limit boundary.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The scan was incomplete: two invalid specs were unread and one debt item was uncovered. No marker was found in the changed accepted-limit implementation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The brief says closeout-check requires completion of the review; no attestation is recorded in this run.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The brief says review-check requires completion of the review; no attestation is recorded in this run.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The required surface check completed with one target, 236 results and zero findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The required rerun could not create Go work/cache files in the read-only sandbox; the sealed bundle's pose-mcp build evidence is pass.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The required module rerun was blocked by the read-only Go work/cache paths; the sealed full pose-mcp unit result is pass, and the focused review tests also passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran and selected backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\"}}\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-cd0ac9394ca5892b.events.ndjson:14:{\"v\":1,\"seq\":14,\"kind\":\"tool_output\",\"tool\":\"shell\",\"text\":\"… review-bundles/rvb-0268e39f3711f7f3.json     | 3764 ++++++++++++++++++\\n .pose/review-bundles/rvb-22f660b39d436e8c.json     | 3770 ++++++++++++++++++\\n .pose/review-bundles/rvb-34dee7b8928be885.json     | 3770 ++++++++++++++++++\\n .pose/review-bundles/rvb-d89a1063ed5e1278.json     | 3771 ++++++++++++++++++\\n .pose/review-conclusions/rrn-07b6541ca424d00b.json |   13 +\\n .pose/review-conclusions/rrn-ef9e246dc33016a0.json |   15 +\\n .pose/review-conclusions/rrn-fa6a6e8e1df0a0ba.json |   13 +\\n .pose/review-run-ledger/rrn-07b6541ca424d00b.json  |    8 +\\n .pose/review-run-ledger/rrn-9d5816c780952f13.json  |    8 +\\n .pose/review-run-ledger/rrn-ef9e246dc33016a0.json  |    8 +\\n .pose/review-run-ledger/rrn-fa6a6e8e1df0a0ba.json  |    8 +\\n ...fb5fa918e9997927459a0b02f5e1df79770871b3fa.json |   23 +\\n ...b23e8e6724d804667c5f0549f877b043472d6e2e94.json |   23 +\\n ...7d16a150c1262d2f53af878b4c8929d7a7