R1-N1, R1-N2 and R1-N3 are fixed, with evidence in the draft. I swept all 18 changed paths, traced accepted-limit parsing, ADR readiness, composite limit IDs, plan and bundle sealing/digests, brief v11, finding conversion and blockers, closeout, documentation and scaffold parity, and checked the L1/L2 justifications.\n\n\"'```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\n      \"line\": 29,\n      \"summary\": \"The accepted-limit reason regex treats punctuation-only text such as '\"'..' as a reason, allowing an unjustified limit through ready-check, and rejects a valid reason beginning with a one-character token. R4's justification gate can therefore false-pass.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:87\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-N2\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:29\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:1212\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed all 18 changed paths. Traced parsing, ADR coverage, qualified IDs across composite scopes, plan and bundle serialization/digests, brief v11, draft-to-attestation conversion, within-limit blockers, closeout, docs and scaffold parity. Checked the prior findings and the L1/L2 justification, and ran the focused accepted-limit, brief and conclusion tests.\\\",\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected the sealed L1/L2 declarations, parser, plan/bundle sealing and conclusion gate. Composite limit attribution and post-seal behavior are verified; L1's author-written scope and L2's post-seal edit boundary are disclosed and justified residual risks. The reason parser defect means R4 does not reliably separate justified assumptions from unsupported ones.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed the added parsing and conclusion flow: this change adds immutable review data and no shared mutable state, asynchronous work, or new cancellation/lifecycle path. The sealed pose-mcp unit suite passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The new review-brief/11 contract carries the sealed limit and finding attribution, while empty optional fields remain omitted. The sealed integration contract test passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The plan, bundle, brief and attestation consumers are connected through the existing review flow. The integration assessment's unobserved HTTP consumers are outside these changed review-limit paths; the sealed bundle-convergence integration passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Parser failures return a specific accepted-limit diagnostic and the conclusion gate returns a blocker naming an unsealed limit or missing rationale. The sealed pose-mcp unit suite passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The brief contract advances to version 11; new fields are omitted when empty, preserving prior plan and bundle serialization, and ADR coverage was updated for qualified IDs. Reviewed the version/digest tests and the sealed immutable-template integration.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-fe37c63d799a5f85\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1 is implemented by parsing once and sealing accepted limits in the plan and bundle; R2 exposes that snapshot in brief v11; R3 records a distinct within-limit disposition; R4 checks reasons and ADR references. D1 assigns semantic scope judgment to the reviewer and requires a sealed ID plus rationale; D2 binds the limits to the plan digest and omits empty fields. The design assessment reported no structural deltas.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed English and Portuguese manual/scaffold copies against runtime behavior: the documents describe the v11 sealed limits and qualified IDs consistently; the sealed template parity integration passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-fe37c63d799a5f85\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation stays within accepted-limit parsing, review-plan/bundle sealing, brief, conclusion and readiness lint behavior named by the spec. The design assessment found no structural deltas.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed the input and authority boundary. A within-limit finding must name an ID sealed in that bundle and carry a rationale; an unsealed ID blocks approval. D1 leaves whether a finding semantically falls within a limit to the reviewer, and the brief exposes the declared limit for that judgment. No path or new authority input is introduced.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-fe37c63d799a5f85\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A shared parser and optional plan/bundle fields are the smallest sufficient path to carry the same declared limit through readiness, review and closeout; the v11 template makes the new reviewer decision explicit. Omitting empty fields preserves old digests. A documentation-only alternative would not seal or validate the limit. D1 would need reconsideration if semantic membership were required to be machine-proven rather than reviewer-judged; that is not this spec's choice.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the required command through the dispatched engine; it exited 0. It selected change set cs-6ba3782f7f26 with head 7bd205c0b1df58cafda4a04b323845223ca1b6c7 rather than this brief's change set/head and reported repository-wide orphan warnings, so it is recorded as a successful command invocation, not as scoped proof of this change.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-fe37c63d799a5f85\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The design assessment passed and reported no structural deltas.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the recommended discovery assessment for pose-mcp; it completed and discovered the component.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the integration assessment. Its unobserved HTTP consumer paths are outside the changed review-limit flow; the sealed relevant bundle-convergence integration passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The assessment was incomplete because two unrelated specs could not be read and it reported one uncovered repository debt marker; this does not identify a defect in the changed paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred because this check requires the review conclusion to be recorded; this run must not record an attestation.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred because this check requires the review conclusion to be recorded; this run must not record an attestation.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the recommended component review suggestion; it selected backend, security and documentation review areas.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The strict surface check passed for the relevant target; the sealed lint-spec gate integration covers the exposed readiness command.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the required command; this read-only sandbox prevented Go build/cache writes before validation completed. The sealed build evidence passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the required module command; this read-only sandbox prevented Go build/cache writes before validation completed. Sealed pose-mcp unit evidence passes, and the focused accepted-limit/brief/conclusion tests passed in this run.\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\"'```\nPOSE_DRAFT_INPUT'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
